g++ --std=c++20 -c main.cpp -I/usr/include/SFML-3.0.2/include && g++ main.o -o App -L/usr/include/SFML-3.0.2/lib -lsfml-graphics -lsfml-window -lsfml-system -lsfml-audio && export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/include/SFML-3.0.2/lib && ./App


This project was the fruit of an idea I had to select GUI elements using a hidden colored texture essentially acting as a giant array to be polled using the cursor coordinates

The boxes are selected using this naive (but successful) method. A newer and faster version is currently implemented in a GUI project I'm still working on. Feel free to poke around the code though!
